            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_d90e5fe8" xml:lang="de">Die Liebe Gottes ist ausgegoßen</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_235683aa">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_e2f451b3">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_1b6a4f0c">
               <date xml:id="date_b2457df8"/>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_3708d4c7">
               <p xml:id="idm82">The present cantata for small orchestra composed for Pentecost is one of the very few of Scheibe's sacred cantatas that has survived (the work is not list in the printed catalogue and it should be placed between SchW B2:028 and B2:029). The work, placed in a dark-bluish folder, was produced by a professional copyist and might have been obtained from the Breitkopf publishers, though it is not listed in their catalogues. Originally the folder also included part material which seems to have been lost after the title was pasted on the front cover sometime in the twentieth century. It is possible that the cantata is among those early works performed at Neukirche in Leipzig by <persName xml:id="idm83" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>. Scheibe's text source is most likely <persName xml:id="idm84" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Johann Knauer</persName>'s <rend xml:id="idm85" fontstyle="italic">Gott-geheiligtes Singen und Spielen des Friedensteinischen</rend> Zions (Gotha, 1721).</p>
            </history>
